.TH "smplay" "1" "2026-01-06" "1.0.0-beta2" "SpectMorph Manual"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
smplay - Program to play a SpectMorph model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]smplay\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]SM-File|SMSet-File\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]smplay\f[R] is a command line based player for SpectMorph models
(which can be created using \f[B]smenc\f[R]).
Playing can use the audio card, so that the model will be heard
directly, or create a wav file instead if the \f[B]--export\f[R] option
is used.
.PP
Since the SpectMorph model consists of sine waves and noise, options to
disable one of these components exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\f[B]smplay\f[R] follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long
options starting with two dashes (\[aq]-\[aq]).
.TP
\f[B]-h\f[R], \f[B]--help\f[R]
Shows a brief help message.
.TP
\f[B]-v\f[R], \f[B]--version\f[R]
Prints out \f[B]smplay\f[R] version.
.TP
\f[B]--rate\f[R] \f[I]\f[VI]<sampling-rate>\f[I]\f[R]
Set replay rate manually; also useful for specifying the desired rate of
the wav file, if \f[B]--export\f[R] is used.
.TP
\f[B]--no-noise\f[R]
Disable noise decoder, so that only the sine wave part of the signal is
decoded.
.TP
\f[B]--no-sines\f[R]
Disable sine decoder, so that only the noise part of the signal is
decoded.
.TP
\f[B]--det-random\f[R]
Use deterministic random generator; this will produce identical noise
components if the same file is decoded twice, making the audio output
exactly the same.
.TP
\f[B]--export\f[R] \f[I]\f[VI]<wav-filename>\f[I]\f[R]
Instead of playing the file, write the output to a wav file.
.TP
\f[B]-m\f[R], \f[B]--midi-note\f[R] \f[I]\f[VI]<midi-note>\f[I]\f[R]
Select midi note to play, in case an SMSet-File was specified as input
file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
smenc.1
